      "claim": "The closest analog, [11C]-JW642, showed moderate BBB penetration by PET in mice with SUV values of 0.2–0.8, supporting meaningful CNS access after systemic administration.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C07"],
      "claim": "Phenylethylmalonamide rapidly appeared in serum and CSF with a CSF/serum ratio of 1.06 in rats, directly demonstrating ready blood-brain barrier penetration.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C06"],
      "claim": "3-[18F]FEPB showed low non-receptor-mediated brain uptake in rodent tissue distribution studies, indicating an impermeable BBB phenotype in one related molecule.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "Most direct in-vivo CNS exposure evidence among structurally related molecules supports meaningful BBB penetration, including PET uptake, CSF/serum equilibration, and good brain/plasma exposure; one related radiotracer showed low brain uptake, but the overall transferable record favors pass.",
